<clause id="_920ce6a8-be2a-52df-ec29-7fd1ae4cb4c1" obligation="normative">
<title id="_c2617228-8179-2304-795b-6f54f0ef807a">Abstract GeoSciML Lite XML Requirements Class (Normative)</title>
<requirement id="_d5cf93b0-6154-191a-031b-152d08de7305" anchor="req_class_gsmljson-lite" model="ogc" type="class">
<title>Requirements Class ‘Abstract GeoSciML Lite JSON’</title><identifier>https://www.opengis.net/spec/geosciml-part3/5.0/req/gsmljson-lite</identifier><subject>Data instance</subject><inherit>https://www.opengis.net/spec/geosciml-part1/5.0/req/gsml-lite</inherit><inherit>/req/gsmljson-core</inherit><inherit>GML Simple Feature OGC 10-100r3 SF-0</inherit><requirement id="_6c64b089-cd6e-be2f-e500-23902b8d095b" model="ogc" type="general"> <identifier>/req/gsmljson-lite/SF-0</identifier></requirement><recommendation id="_e9ad582e-5f15-3e2b-fc06-c808c04f5d58" model="ogc" type="general"> <identifier>/rec/gsmljson-lite/SF-0-simpletype</identifier></recommendation><recommendation id="_3686925b-abaa-64bc-5e9e-1e598f2cab61" model="ogc" type="general"> <identifier>/rec/gsmljson-lite/user-json</identifier></recommendation><recommendation id="_0f0e3643-9bca-288f-9f80-ebcbe4cc94bf" model="ogc" type="general"> <identifier>/rec/gsmljson-lite/user-ns</identifier></recommendation>

</requirement>

<p id="_d3664aff-f4b5-861c-57c6-deeefc9abccf">The abstract GeoSciML Lite encoding sets general encoding rules for XML targets, regardless of version of GML.</p>

<clause id="_cbf7eaee-938d-ce6e-951c-8cdf17ed0b65" obligation="normative">
<title id="_b361291a-d1f5-0ea4-fddb-1fc933d82f5a">Simple Feature</title>
<p id="_f36d7017-1988-f541-c23e-44020d329df9">GeoSciML Lite schemas are meant to deliver simple content, consistent with simple scenarios described in GML Simple Feature Level 0 (OGC 10-100r3).  User defined properties must respect the same constrains as defined in SF-0 specification.</p>

<requirement id="_0b7aa04a-d013-7056-85c7-0ef94aded51b" anchor="req_gsmljson_lite_SF0" model="ogc"> <identifier>/req/gsmljson-lite/SF-0</identifier><component id="_2f4b359c-363a-542c-ca14-717e58baa73b" class="part"><p id="_335e3050-ed34-efba-41a8-16d62324ebae">An XML instance document SHALL be compliant to GML Simple Feature Level 0.</p>
</component>
</requirement>

<p id="_b2140f50-bd2f-23b8-0f2e-b6523e365739">Simple Feature defines 3 compliance levels summarized in Table17.</p>

<table id="_1425e434-22d9-427d-1c2e-0cc633e7fc56" width="100%"><colgroup><col width="36%"/><col width="18%"/><col width="23%"/><col width="23%"/></colgroup>
<name id="_e1b2d63e-aa5d-89aa-19ac-f88fbee427af">Reproduction of Table 1 of 10-100r3 (Clause 2.1)</name>
<thead><tr id="_332635cf-a294-b2ea-105b-bc6b518a8bef"><th id="_cfdf91da-f93d-d1f2-21af-50bb834762ac" valign="middle" align="center"><strong> </strong></th>
<th id="_9597829c-b610-fed7-cf7b-875491a1f92c" valign="middle" align="center"><strong>Level SF-0</strong></th>
<th id="_c3ed9ed9-5375-65d4-b42a-d63a9f303f7a" valign="middle" align="center"><strong>Level SF-1</strong></th>
<th id="_e6628d70-1b29-4d88-3afb-068ec049f827" valign="middle" align="center"><strong>Level SF-2</strong></th>
</tr></thead>
<tbody><tr id="_8c12462e-2c3f-ba8d-044f-f439fc50b787"><td id="_24a9dec6-4788-b886-ba95-c5fe9cb78d9c" valign="middle" align="center"><p id="_fa91db37-a7cc-b568-2ed6-b62990e2a007">restricted set of built-in nonspatial</p>

<p id="_dc7fb33e-6108-6887-352e-506e311d316f">property types</p>
</td>
<td id="_0aca1ff3-ab6e-0c1c-51ac-90530898e01b" valign="middle" align="center">Yes<sup>1</sup></td>
<td id="_ddf407a0-3931-5ceb-3478-aca9da0d0644" valign="middle" align="center">Yes<sup>1</sup></td>
<td id="_b3884355-d481-2672-cbd1-2db46f0912bb" valign="middle" align="center">No</td>
</tr><tr id="_ab1c9da5-3e17-d1c8-9593-656f103f747b"><td id="_04aad6fd-16de-9233-061a-b1d9cd64beaf" valign="middle" align="center">Restricted set of property-types</td>
<td id="_4627f3d8-5568-ea51-4a34-3f9bf9723f66" valign="middle" align="center">Yes<sup>2</sup></td>
<td id="_08d6503b-acc4-4eed-d2dc-a693f5d4435f" valign="middle" align="center">Yes<sup>2</sup></td>
<td id="_314022f3-f71d-3d15-b60d-64fedc104149" valign="middle" align="center">Yes<sup>2</sup></td>
</tr><tr id="_0aa7c00b-cf27-c929-7b07-e8a225920699"><td id="_b44ef898-7925-783e-6152-3485eaa5a8e2" valign="middle" align="center">user-defined property types</td>
<td id="_b099042d-bd25-78ba-718c-07f3b4160c56" valign="middle" align="center">No</td>
<td id="_8e704cab-b496-cf3f-e32f-3eb6cea93ca5" valign="middle" align="center">Yes</td>
<td id="_e8937c48-5786-3db3-0448-b3d7af388c86" valign="middle" align="center">Yes</td>
</tr><tr id="_d4b8c057-a710-3c4d-6998-72c42d408f64"><td id="_9f0e1673-3b73-d448-9b91-921b87731214" valign="middle" align="center">use of nillable and xsi:nil</td>
<td id="_9e53fd27-b451-b8a6-62ce-f159559afeb9" valign="middle" align="center">No</td>
<td id="_246f946e-88b4-8bcd-03ff-b81bc737802b" valign="middle" align="center">Yes</td>
<td id="_1d190a15-582d-39e2-3b81-6bce8fe94e71" valign="middle" align="center">Yes</td>
</tr><tr id="_89c1a591-a8e3-e8b1-26b7-d0d2eae2cd6a"><td id="_b22f828e-40bb-9874-b3b8-4e117bc8afd8" valign="middle" align="center">cardinality of properties</td>
<td id="_8c7ae8b0-4861-504b-0919-ef7a86ab7efd" valign="middle" align="center">0..1</td>
<td id="_454a8a62-5b62-2519-f02a-93d61967e739" valign="middle" align="center">0..unbounded</td>
<td id="_ceea8312-8a63-6ad7-be21-ca173fee38da" valign="middle" align="center">0..unbounded</td>
</tr><tr id="_b20638a2-6fd5-3b2c-83af-24939e1132e8"><td id="_c89ccc75-f957-9f16-3f7d-a84e2c0b8662" valign="middle" align="center"><p id="_98133e0d-5804-0f92-0739-689ab6b3e029">non-spatial property values</p>

<p id="_2545c1b4-c52f-d422-9352-c300617107fd">references</p>
</td>
<td id="_a3e2965e-4d03-9402-6983-2d18d871fd6d" valign="middle" align="center">Yes<sup>3</sup></td>
<td id="_a70d7b1e-440c-f701-fe8b-1fa9bdc6879a" valign="middle" align="center">Yes<sup>3</sup></td>
<td id="_e73df011-d5ed-602e-989a-246d9804020e" valign="middle" align="center">Yes</td>
</tr><tr id="_fa99b6a2-d66a-cf63-b982-d00a8e56e100"><td id="_638cc70f-9ec6-2846-27b8-78442d65fcae" valign="middle" align="center"><p id="_b802d81a-b192-bce2-1108-cc86e35f82ec">spatial property values</p>

<p id="_f49e4bd0-2c1a-ea8c-c9f1-058624b509d0">references</p>
</td>
<td id="_86e6ec5d-05d6-6b0d-3282-2fd139b6f681" valign="middle" align="center">Yes<sup>3</sup></td>
<td id="_2531885d-0ee9-b70f-340a-51d50aead6fb" valign="middle" align="center">Yes<sup>3</sup></td>
<td id="_0a5f9a0d-4365-6e2b-f718-2a7be6249729" valign="middle" align="center">Yes</td>
</tr><tr id="_a27039ee-cd0b-828d-2a88-ff5f56d07add"><td id="_d6bf3c69-4b92-b1d0-5306-15899cf6b785" valign="middle" align="center"><ol id="_ad4b167c-da09-3aa5-975a-d1485b9737a5" type="arabic"><li><p id="_45a8dec3-8c8b-8df3-05dd-421ac36dbbd0">string, integer, me<strong>a</strong>surement, date, real, binary, boolean, URI</p>
</li>
<li><p id="_854eca17-4b72-0f19-80b0-9a5b6f369fdd">Point, Curve (LineString), Surface (Polygon), Geometry, MultiPoint, MultiCurve, MultiSurface, MultiGeometry</p>
</li>
<li><p id="_8c512655-e805-2a03-a25c-92120da0623a">In levels 0 and 1, remote values for properties are supported <strong>only </strong>through the use of the type gml:ReferenceType. The more generalized GML property-type pattern allowing mixed inline and byReference encoded property values within the same instance document is disallowed.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</td>
<td id="_e65841fc-ed4f-3ad2-2b01-90baf0035abf" valign="middle" align="center"/><td id="_f7e7688b-4a81-543c-6cc9-98bf240e94dc" valign="middle" align="center"/><td id="_00965cf5-9ac4-3f80-ef86-0dcc198e7aa3" valign="middle" align="center"/></tr></tbody>
</table>
</clause>

<clause id="_26faf8f0-9c89-3407-7ffa-2a1cd76bf766" obligation="normative">
<title id="_d0ca207f-0187-3b04-a7b9-49e17d48193c">Simple Content</title>
<p id="_1939c7fe-0047-f59e-95f9-c7f2155158a9">SF-0 allows the definition of complex content (Clause 9.3.2 of OGC 10-100r3). To be consistent with the most common scenario encountered in GIS which is a direct mapping from a database table to XML, this specification recommends that user defined content be restricted to simple type.</p>

<p id="_e8a9903b-87bb-c741-79d4-5f94e2a1a61d">Unresolved directive in sections/clause_6_normative_text.adoc — include::/recommendations/lite-json/REC_lite_SF0_simpletype.adoc[]</p>

<p id="_c95bd8c7-ae4c-cf98-4eec-fab4a27b22ed">GeoSciML Lite allows user defined properties to be appended at the end of the list of feature properties using xsd:any</p>

<sourcecode id="_58c63260-7497-0dc3-c279-832fd96683c2" lang="xml" unnumbered="true"><body>&lt;any processContents="lax" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"&gt;
      &lt;annotation&gt;
            &lt;documentation&gt;A placeholder allowing any user-defined
                attributes to be delivered in addition to those specified above.&lt;/documentation&gt;
      &lt;/annotation&gt;
&lt;/any&gt;</body></sourcecode>


<p id="_9733f1c7-bc75-caff-4213-059eeec7b559">Process content is set to “lax”, which means the validator will attempt to validate user defined property only if a schema is.  To help client applications and developers to validate instance containing user defined properties, a XSD schema should be provided in the instance’s schemaLocation attribute.</p>

<p id="_9f689386-254c-20bd-0b54-a55023d5e92e">Unresolved directive in sections/clause_6_normative_text.adoc — include::/recommendations/lite-json/REC_lite_user_json.adoc[]</p>
</clause>

<clause id="_e953c071-d9eb-cc9a-81da-73338e773ace" obligation="normative">
<title id="_22da67b0-0e4b-55d6-fe4b-1b375a6b853e">User Defined Namespaces</title>
<p id="_2fa79132-ba3f-bb7f-d435-cfc18b8e494f">This specification does not prescribe if the user types are to be defined in GeoSciML Lite namespace or using a different namespace.  It is understood that this might be constrained by the technology used to generate the instance.  But to avoid potential conflict with future minor changes to GeoSciML Lite, or name conflicts when aggregating results from many sources, it is recommended that the data providers, or the community, use different namespaces, if possible.</p>

<p id="_79b11b3a-368d-0e52-4b54-992212900065">Unresolved directive in sections/clause_6_normative_text.adoc — include::/recommendations/lite-json/REC_lite_user_ns.adoc[]</p>
</clause>
</clause>

<clause id="_1c84ac26-b9c5-0a65-00f3-2e08a821a61b" obligation="normative">
<title id="_90ba80e7-5735-b8b0-e229-babf235bcd11">GeoSciML Lite GML 3.1 profile (Normative)</title>
<requirement id="_bcab8da3-b115-a7c3-2f5d-335a9cfbd78d" anchor="req_class_gsmljson-lite31" model="ogc" type="class">
<title>Requirements Class ‘GeoSciML Lite GML 3.1 profile’</title><identifier>https://www.opengis.net/spec/geosciml-part3/5.0/req/gsmljson-lite-31</identifier><subject>Data instance</subject><inherit>https://www.opengis.net/spec/geosciml-part1/5.0/req/gsml-lite</inherit><inherit>/req/gsmljson-lite</inherit><requirement id="_b02b06e4-6aea-3ae9-7d7c-80a7028156cc" model="ogc" type="general"> <identifier>/req/gsmljson-lite-31/json</identifier></requirement>

</requirement>

<p id="_a66f768f-6a3b-6ffb-38f9-02a3212fab1f">Because of the limited availability of WFS 2.0 compliant servers and clients, GeoSciML SWG officially supports WFS 1.1.0 and GML 3.1.1 for delivery of Lite features. </p>

<p id="_d29a2278-7889-3c4e-e577-bfb35e5d6447">All the elements from the GeoSciML Lite package must be schema valid according to the XSD document provided at <link target="http://schemas.opengis.net/gsml/4.1/geosciml-lite.xsd"/>.</p>

<requirement id="_adc07fdb-0d89-6d0f-b008-469ae9f776ea" anchor="req_gsmljson_lite_31_xsd" model="ogc"> <identifier>/req/gsmljson-lite-31/xsd</identifier><component id="_6fa345bc-4f5b-439e-b157-7dcdb5fdeaa6" class="part"><p id="_13901791-826f-1af7-d010-fd29be5646a6">An XML instance document shall validate with schema located at   <link target="http://schemas.opengis.net/gsml/4.1/geosciml-portrayal.xsd"/>.</p>
</component>
</requirement>
</clause>
</clause>

<clause id="_3c7de26d-f675-24f6-8f2a-05229231d4a7" obligation="normative">
<title id="_924d9443-22c3-a2bc-48bd-0899d3683af9">Media Types for any data encoding(s)</title>
<p id="_d6304c3a-41cb-cb21-f447-30c28e46f8f6">GeoSciML 5.0 data conforming to the logical model defined in Part 1 of GeoSciML can be encoded in documents conforming to JSON-FG.  The standard MIME-type and sub-type for JSON-FG data should be used to indicate the encoding in internet exchange, as specified in <link target="https://docs.ogc.org/is/21-045r1/21-045r1.html#media-types">OGC 21-045r1</link>,_ namely</p>

<p id="_c1af95a0-bbb4-6d3b-2aee-4bf65684ef04"><tt>application/geo+json</tt></p>
</clause>








</sections><annex id="_7ffc4e3f-4c1a-0e73-b2a3-7d5b1c4ce84d" obligation="informative">
<title id="_0ae400d0-fc5b-94a1-586c-a20b12ca10c6">Conformance Class Abstract Test Suite (Normative)</title>
<note id="_63e4b0a0-3d94-7020-361f-fcac21929de5"><p id="_e3b4abfb-677c-1601-a95d-8eb60217c3f8">Ensure that there is a conformance class for each requirements class and a test for each requirement (identified by requirement name and number)</p>
</note>

<clause id="_5509d42a-02e9-d5df-a903-9a7a23727bab" obligation="informative">
<title id="_e687ec7b-c3e0-9926-7832-77ede3a8f561">Conformance Class A</title>
<requirement id="_decc1f24-9f68-e133-ed15-0a9d614f68c6" anchor="ats_example1" model="ogc" type="conformanceclass"> <identifier>http://www.opengis.net/spec/name-of-standard/1.0/conf/example1</identifier><classification><tag>Target Type</tag><value>Web API</value></classification><classification><tag>target</tag><value>http://www.opengis.net/spec/ABCD/m.n/req/req-class-a</value></classification><requirement id="_ff77108c-a8f6-08c6-601e-e28822716dd7" model="ogc" type="abstracttest"> <identifier>/conf/core/map-response</identifier></requirement><requirement id="_e72c02a8-3296-118e-700f-50a080090cc6" model="ogc" type="abstracttest"> <identifier>/conf/core/http</identifier></requirement>
</requirement>

<clause id="_95170162-0a0f-09f5-cd34-24d3c5f42816" obligation="informative">
<title id="_260450a4-1b11-9c40-f0c3-9020d5927560">Example 1</title>
<requirement id="_da859a71-6085-ad51-19c2-5aa9f162f1ba" anchor="ats_core_api-definition-op" model="ogc" type="abstracttest"> <identifier>/conf/core/map-response</identifier><classification><tag>target</tag><value>/req/req-class-a/req-name-1</value></classification><component id="_85c56698-5fb3-60d7-84c0-9a8dc916a839" class="test-purpose"><p id="_8f5557b7-9b6a-5dd2-4976-db599b7e4496">Verify that the implementation’s response for the map retrieval operation is correct</p>
</component><component id="_1dec5d8d-6407-cf6e-42cc-39bdec221c22" class="test-method"><p id="_f110e3a8-8d6f-3aeb-cd60-cfd8b7247cac">A single step test method can be documented as a single line.</p>
</component>
</requirement>
</clause>

<clause id="_82e8b1bf-9c75-b737-7086-c7d15e69e1fe" obligation="informative">
<title id="_16a1d527-9574-b57f-20ad-95c86008da16">Example 2</title>
<requirement id="_d534372c-f008-6390-da90-8fd2ffddd13e" anchor="ats_core_http" model="ogc" type="abstracttest"> <identifier>/conf/core/http</identifier><classification><tag>target</tag><value>/req/req-class-a/req-name-2</value></classification><component id="_75e6681c-8759-7d88-5a6e-fd3924459723" class="test-purpose"><p id="_d8c68c9c-a138-50a6-08e1-d7f10bbdfeba">Validate that the resource paths advertised through the API conform with HTTP 1.1 and, where appropriate, TLS.</p>
</component>

<component exclude="false" class="test method"><component exclude="false" class="step"><p id="_89bea33c-5ef2-cb52-41a9-e90e99335d26">A sequential multi-step test method can be documented as shown here. This is the first step.</p>
</component>
<component exclude="false" class="step"><p id="_bb001deb-dabb-cfdc-769d-73ac6f6eef2e">This is the second step.</p>
</component></component></requirement>
</clause>
</clause>
</annex><annex id="_96ac1666-e590-c0bc-6189-9b06cae0e238" obligation="informative">
<title id="_fb5be62a-e0b1-f53e-52fb-f043c7f262f3">Title</title>
<note id="_159a4ec6-3751-b292-9d8b-e31170a42309"><p id="_0e5dcb8f-837e-641a-a3be-7dd168610057">Place other Annex material in sequential annexes beginning with “B” and leave final two annexes for the Revision History and Bibliography</p>
</note>
</annex><annex id="_86ce8e65-c445-b308-465c-eba6a1493662" obligation="informative">
